WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
Think about this: Which brief is easiest
to audit?

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:05.100
Let’s work through it together.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:10.420
I'm Doctor Gainz. Lesson 20: Build a
source-constrained case brief.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:15.800
A useful case brief separates confirmed
facts, estimates, questions, and

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.920
next actions. Every financial figure
should carry a label, source, effective

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.360
date, and reviewer status.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:26.620
Keep the original document reference
beside the summary so another person

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.940
can check it without reconstructing your
reasoning.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:34.300
Use this original prompt with fictional or
authorized material: “Summarize

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.740
only the supplied records.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:41.060
Create sections for process, authority,
accounting, events, unresolved

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:42.700
issues, and requested review.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:45.760
Attach source references. Mark conflicts.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:50.660
Do not search for private people,
fabricate missing data, rank legal rights,

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:55.480
or contact anyone.” Check the result line
by line before sharing it.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.400
Be especially careful with current-tense
statements.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.060
“The ledger recorded a deposit on a date”
is different from “The money

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:07.280
remains available.” A brief should
preserve that distinction and make stale

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.580
sources easy to spot.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:10.480
Pause and try this.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.420
Write a one-page fictional brief with two
source-linked facts, one estimate,

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:19.080
three unresolved questions, and a specific
handoff request.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:23.300
Quick knowledge check. Which brief is
easiest to audit?

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.360
The answer: A structured summary
separating sourced facts and unresolved

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:33.200
questions. Source references and clear
uncertainty let a reviewer verify the

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.900
work. Keep the source, the date, and the
unknowns visible.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:38.720
I'll see you in the next lesson.
